  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Shared site Q505617 identifies this ancient entrance within park way304804695. Four integral piers are independently mapped as ways304818582,304818577,304818576 and304818580/native35184676907414,35184676907409,35184676907408 and35184676907412. Anchor uses the inner eastern pier way304818576; the other three retain their exact offsets. Internal +X follows the outer-pier row east/slightly south and +Z points south/slightly west across the approach. Native east/up/south axes are baked with heading0. Only the four pier records are replaced; all three passages and every other mapped building remain.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Photo-led medium-fi broken masonry exterior. No qualified mapped heights. Working low-body heights west-to-east1.75/2.15/2.30/1.90m, with a4.05m narrow remnant at the eastern pier, follow the ordinary entrance picture as approximate visual controls. Bases follow the original standard terrain; top erosion and rubble facets are original reconstructed geometry. Exact historic elevations, surviving fracture patterns, stone/block inventories and hidden faces are unverified. Do not infer intact arches or copied inscriptions from this model."
  },
